  "evidence": "Traced the abelian tower estimate to its ambiguous coinvariant index, the invariant characters and their uniform base-field bound. Checked the separate Stickelberger and reflection/signature inputs at their actual call sites.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "ACI-01",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "A base-field character count bounds the relative class coinvariants",
      "anchor": "inputs-ambiguous-class-characters",
      "statement": "Let F contain μ_ℓ and K=F(μ_{ℓ^n}) be totally complex with Gal(K/F) cyclic generated by τ. With C=Cl(𝒪_K), the index [C:ℓC+(1−τ)C] is bounded by the number B_F of continuous 𝔽_ℓ-valued G_F-characters unramified at all finite places away from ℓ.",
      "hypotheses": "ℓ is prime and F is a number field. A primitive ℓth root in F supplies the Kummer finiteness argument. Local conditions above ℓ are unrestricted in the definition of B_F. In the Hilbert class comparison over K the character on U=G_K is invariant and unramified at every finite place; the total complexity of K meets the archimedean hypothesis.",
      "definitions": [
        "The quotient Q=C/(ℓC+(1−τ)C) consists of the coinvariants of C/ℓC.",
        "For the finite space E of invariant unramified characters on U, N is the intersection of their kernels in U. Then U/N lies in the centre of the finite group G_F/N, whose quotient by U/N is cyclic.",
        "For a finite abelian group D, |Hom(D,𝔽_ℓ)|=|D[ℓ]|. Applying the inclusion (U/N)[ℓ]→(G_F/N)[ℓ] compares cardinalities."
      ],
      "equations": [
        "inputs-ambiguous-class-quotient"
      ],
      "dependencies": [
        "ART-02"
      ],
